<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Entitlements for the Swift app binary. Deliberately minimal: this file must
  NOT gain disable-library-validation. That relaxation belongs only on the
  bundled interpreter (see python-entitlements.plist); the app links nothing
  outside /System and /usr/lib and keeps library validation fully enforced.

  No apple-events. It was here from 2026-08-13 on the belief that reconnecting
  the NAS drove the Finder; it doesn't. The reconnect is a bare `mount volume`
  (BackupEngine.mountScriptArguments), which sends no Apple Event, so Kept
  never needs Automation. Verified 2026-10-13: a build without this
  entitlement reconnected an ejected share in under a second.

  photos-library: under the hardened runtime, an app that doesn't declare it
  is refused the Photos permission without macOS ever asking. That's why the
  Photos prompt never appeared in August 2026, and why Kept needed Full Disk
  Access until 2026-11-18. With it, the Photos permission (Full Access) lets
  Kept and osxphotos read the library's files: tested that day with a
  separate app signed the same way, which read Photos.sqlite and exported 5
  photos with no Full Disk Access.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.personal-information.photos-library</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
